WEBVTT

NOTE Chapter-aligned captions from the TTS script. Within-chapter cue timing is approximate.

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.673
A calendar shows when you’re busy. It rarely shows which

00:00:03.673 --> 00:00:07.246
promises depend on each other. For a student balancing exams,

00:00:07.246 --> 00:00:10.820
interviews, and club responsibilities, one changed date can break the

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:14.393
whole week. Dira connects those commitments and helps repair the

00:00:14.393 --> 00:00:14.750
consequences.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:19.779
Here’s a synthetic student week. The professor moves Friday’s exam

00:00:19.779 --> 00:00:24.457
to Wednesday. That leaves too little preparation time, breaks the

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:29.136
recovery buffer before an interview, and conflicts with club work.

00:00:29.136 --> 00:00:33.814
Dira’s feasibility engine exposes all three problems. Available slack drops

00:00:33.814 --> 00:00:34.750
below zero.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:40.380
NVIDIA Nemotron Super, running on Nebius Token Factory, interprets the

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:45.661
email. Ultra proposes structured repair candidates. Deterministic code checks their

00:00:45.661 --> 00:00:50.941
sources, feasibility, and policy before selecting a plan. This deliberately

00:00:50.941 --> 00:00:56.222
malicious candidate cites a nonexistent message. Dira rejects it before

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:56.750
execution.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:02.411
The plan proposes rebooking the interview, moving flexible work, rebuilding

00:01:02.411 --> 00:01:07.722
study time, and delegating the club task. Delegation requires my

00:01:07.722 --> 00:01:13.032
approval. Dira pauses the entire plan here. The independent surface

00:01:13.032 --> 00:01:16.750
comparison confirms that nothing has changed yet.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:22.694
After I approve, Dira revalidates the plan against fresh state.

00:01:22.694 --> 00:01:28.289
The first interview slot is already taken. Rather than pretending

00:01:28.289 --> 00:01:33.883
it succeeded, Dira observes the failure and replans around another

00:01:33.883 --> 00:01:39.477
offered slot. Each action needs an independent read-back before the

00:01:39.477 --> 00:01:45.072
internal graph is updated. In this run, deterministic planning supplies

00:01:45.072 --> 00:01:46.750
the winning repair.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:51.372
Thirteen actions are verified, and slack returns to positive territory.

00:01:51.372 --> 00:01:55.643
Study time is restored before the exam, flexible work moves,

00:01:55.643 --> 00:01:59.915
and Maya becomes the task owner. The interview request remains

00:01:59.915 --> 00:02:04.187
explicitly marked as awaiting the counterparty. A successful request is

00:02:04.187 --> 00:02:06.750
never presented as someone else’s confirmation.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:12.291
Dira keeps account-specific commitments and private memory across sessions. Confirmed

00:02:12.291 --> 00:02:17.482
corrections can become reusable rules for later plans. You choose

00:02:17.482 --> 00:02:22.674
the connected tools, approval requirements, and messaging policy, and you

00:02:22.674 --> 00:02:24.750
can export your memory.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:28.588
The broker also blocks this forbidden destination and records the

00:02:28.588 --> 00:02:32.076
denial. These demo integrations are simulated; real Google checks are

00:02:32.076 --> 00:02:35.564
documented separately. OpenShell is not active around this hosted app.

00:02:35.564 --> 00:02:39.052
Dira’s goal is simple: help you keep the promises behind

00:02:39.052 --> 00:02:39.750
your calendar.
